{% doc %}
  blocks/accordion-row.liquid

  One row of an **Accordion** — a question, or any other short label, and
  whatever answers it.

  Nothing here is about FAQs. The block was called `faq-row` and lived beside a
  `faq-accordion`, which read as a section-specific pair and kept merchants from
  reaching for it anywhere else. It is a general disclosure row: shipping terms
  under a product, a spec table on a landing page, a "what's included" list in a
  footer column. `question` is still the setting id, because renaming a stored id
  would empty the field on every row already published.

  ## The answer is blocks, not a rich text field

  It used to be one `richtext` setting, which meant an answer could only ever be
  prose. Half the questions a store actually gets are answered better by
  something else — a size table, a delivery banner, an image of the returns
  label, a button to the policy page — and none of that fits in a rich text
  field.

  So the panel is `{% content_for 'blocks' %}` and the row accepts `@theme`:
  every block the theme has is available inside an answer, and the Text block is
  what the preset puts there, so the default row is still a question and a
  paragraph. Nothing here knows what a Text block is.

  ## Still a `<details>`


  The disclosure is native, so the answer is on the page with JavaScript off,
  `<summary>` is already a button with an expanded state to a screen reader, and
  the browser's own in-page search finds the text. Nothing here re-implements
  that with a `<button>` and an `aria-expanded` of its own.

  The open and close motion belongs to `<accordion-element>` in
  `assets/modules.js` — a measured WAAPI height animation that every other
  disclosure group in the theme already uses. This file contributes markup, not a
  second animation system: the panel is a plain wrapper precisely so that
  animation has a single box to measure.

  ## Two icons in one summary, and only one of them means "open"

  The toggle is `snippets/icon.liquid` like everything else — a **plus** whose
  upright bar travels onto the crossbar and stops there as a minus, or a
  **chevron** that turns. It used to be two pseudo-elements crossed in CSS,
  which is the same glyph drawn a second time in a second place.

  The icon beside the question is content, and it does not move at all. That is
  worth stating because it did: the group rule in `assets/base.css` rotated
  every `.icon` inside an open summary, so a truck or a padlock a merchant had
  chosen turned upside down along with the marker. The rule names the chevron
  and the plus now.

  ## The icon is the Subheading block's, by reference

  `blocks/subheading.liquid` settled how an icon is chosen in this theme —
  **None**, **Icon** or **Image**, one field per source, the chosen one shown and
  the others hidden — and the same four setting ids are used here (`icon_source`,
  `icon`, `icon_image`, `icon_image_alt`) so a merchant who has configured a
  Subheading already knows this control. The glyph comes from
  `snippets/icon.liquid` and an upload from `snippets/image.liquid`, which is
  where every other icon and image in the theme comes from.

  Only the box is this file's own, and it is derived rather than configured: the
  merchant sets **Icon size** and the tile around it follows, so the two can
  never disagree.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = block.settings

  assign question = s.question
  assign icon_source = s.icon_source | default: 'none'
  capture icon_px
    render 'icon-size', size: s.icon_size, custom: s.icon_size_custom
  endcapture
  assign icon_size = icon_px | plus: 0

  assign has_icon = false
  if icon_source == 'icon' and s.icon != blank
    assign has_icon = true
  endif
  if icon_source == 'image' and s.icon_image != blank
    assign has_icon = true
  endif

  assign toggle = s.toggle_style | default: 'plus'

  comment
    ---- the frame ----

    One border decision, three lines. The frame around the row, the tile behind
    the leading icon and the tile behind the toggle all take it, because three
    controls for three lines a merchant will always set the same way is three
    chances for them to disagree.

    `none` is a zero width rather than `border-style: none`, so the row keeps
    its box either way and turning the border off does not move the text.
  endcomment
  assign border_style = s.border_style | default: 'none'
  assign border_width = 0
  if border_style != 'none'
    assign border_width = s.border_width | default: 1 | plus: 0

    comment
      With no colour picked the line is `currentColor`, which the colour filters
      cannot take an alpha channel from — there is no channel to read until the
      scheme resolves it in the browser. `color-mix` fades it at that point
      instead, so an unset colour is a hairline rather than a hard rule.
    endcomment
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 20%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_paint = s.border_color
    endif
  endif

  assign radius = s.border_radius | default: 14 | plus: 0

  # The icon tile grows with the glyph rather than taking a second slider that
  # can be set smaller than the thing it contains.
  assign icon_box = icon_size | plus: 12

  comment
    ---- the question's typography ----

    The theme's, by reference, in the three parts every text block here uses:

      the named presets   `.block-text--h4` and its eight siblings in
                          `assets/base.css`, which point `--block-font-*` at the
                          tokens `css-variables.liquid` writes from Theme
                          settings › Typography
      Custom and colour   `snippets/block-typography.liquid`, which emits only
                          what a class cannot know
      the consumption     `.accordion-row__question` in `assets/base.css` reads those
                          properties, with its own values as the fallback

    Not `.block-text` itself. That class also sets `flex` and `inline-size`, and
    this span is a flex item of the summary row already taking the line between
    the icon and the toggle. The typography half is the part worth sharing; the
    layout half belongs to the row.

    Same arrangement and the same setting ids as `blocks/_tab.liquid` — a
    merchant who has styled a tab name has styled a question.

    `default` is the default, so a row saved before this existed emits no class
    that resolves and no declarations, and looks exactly as it did.
  endcomment
  assign preset = s.preset | default: 'default'

  assign question_classes = 'accordion-row__question block-text--' | append: preset
  if s.color == 'gradient'
    assign question_classes = question_classes | append: ' block-text--gradient'
  endif
-%}

{%- capture question_style -%}
  {%- render 'block-typography', block: s -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- if question != blank -%}
  {%- capture row_style -%}
    {%- render 'spacing', block: s, declarations: true -%}
    {%- if has_icon -%}
      --accordion-row-icon-size: {{ icon_size }}px;
      --accordion-row-icon-box: {{ icon_box }}px;
    {%- endif -%}
    --accordion-row-radius: {{ radius }}px;
    {%- if s.background_color != blank -%}
      --accordion-row-background: {{ s.background_color }};
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if border_width > 0 -%}
      --accordion-row-border-width: {{ border_width }}px;
      --accordion-row-border-style: {{ border_style }};
      --accordion-row-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    A row animates as one thing. There is no stagger setting on it, because the
    only two boxes inside are the question and the answer — and the answer is
    hidden until it is opened, so "one after the other" would be a delay on
    nothing. The list cascades from the Accordion above it instead.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <motion-effect
    class="accordion-row-motion"
    {% render 'motion-attrs', kind: 'text', block: s %}
  >
  <details
    class="accordion-row accordion-row--toggle-{{ toggle }}{% if has_icon %} accordion-row--has-icon{% endif %}"
    {% if s.open_by_default %}open data-default-open{% endif %}
    data-block-spacing
    style="{{ row_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <summary class="accordion-row__summary">
      {%- if has_icon -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          No `aria-hidden` on the tile. `snippets/icon.liquid` already hides the
          glyphs it renders, and an upload carries its own **Alt text** field —
          hiding the wrapper would silently discard whatever the merchant typed
          into it. Each source keeps its own semantics, as in the Subheading
          block.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="accordion-row__icon">
          {%- if icon_source == 'image' -%}
            {% render 'image',
               image: s.icon_image,
               alt: s.icon_image_alt,
               sizes: '48px',
               wrapper_class: 'accordion-row__icon-image' %}
          {%- else -%}
            {% render 'icon', icon: s.icon, size: icon_size %}
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}

      <span class="{{ question_classes }}" style="{{ question_style | strip_newlines | strip }}">
        {{- question -}}
      </span>

      {%- comment -%}
        Decorative. `<summary>` conveys the expanded state already, so labelling
        this would announce the same thing twice.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="accordion-row__toggle" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- if toggle == 'arrow' -%}
          {% render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-down', size: 14, class: 'accordion-row__chevron' %}
        {%- else -%}
          {% render 'icon', icon: 'plus', size: 14, class: 'accordion-row__plus' %}
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
    </summary>

    {%- comment -%}
      A plain wrapper, deliberately. `<accordion-element>` animates the height of
      the `<details>` itself and measures this box to find the end value; a
      `grid-template-rows` trick here would animate against that measurement and
      land with a visible jump.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="accordion-row__panel">
      <div class="accordion-row__answer">
        {% content_for 'blocks' %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </details>
  </motion-effect>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.accordion_row.name",
  "tag": null,
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "@theme" },
    { "type": "@app" }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "question",
      "label": "t:blocks.accordion_row.settings.question.label",
      "default": "How long does delivery take?"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "open_by_default",
      "label": "t:blocks.accordion_row.settings.open_by_default.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.accordion_row.settings.open_by_default.info",
      "default": false
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:blocks.subheading.headers.icon" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "t:blocks.accordion_row.paragraphs.icon" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "icon_source",
      "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_source.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.none.label" },
        { "value": "icon", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_source.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "image", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_source.options__3.label" }
      ],
      "default": "icon"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "icon",
      "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "star", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "check", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "heart", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "tag", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__4.label" },
        { "value": "truck", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__5.label" },
        { "value": "refresh", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__6.label" },
        { "value": "lock", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__7.label" },
        { "value": "clock", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__8.label" },
        { "value": "location", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__9.label" },
        { "value": "mail", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__10.label" },
        { "value": "note", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__11.label" },
        { "value": "info", "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon.options__12.label" }
      ],
      "default": "note",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source == 'icon' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "icon_image",
      "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_image.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_image.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "icon_image_alt",
      "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_image_alt.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_image_alt.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "icon_size",
      "label": "t:blocks.subheading.settings.icon_size.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.accordion_row.settings.icon_size.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "extra_small", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "small", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "medium", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "large", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__4.label" },
        { "value": "extra_large", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__5.label" },
        { "value": "custom", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__6.label" }
      ],
      "default": "medium",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "icon_size_custom",
      "label": "t:shared.icon_size.custom.label",
      "info": "t:shared.icon_size.custom.info",
      "min": 12,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 16,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_source != 'none' and block.settings.icon_size == 'custom' }}"
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "t:shared.typography.header" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "t:shared.typography.paragraph" },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "preset", "label": "t:shared.typography.preset.label", "info": "t:shared.typography.preset.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "default", "label": "t:shared.typography.preset.options__1.label" },
